.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt PUSHOVER 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pushover
.Nd send a notification through the Pushover API
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl t Ar title
.Oo Ar user : Oc Ns Ar app
.Ar message
.Nm
.Fl h | Fl V
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
sends
.Ar message
as a Pushover notification from the application
.Ar app
to the user
.Ar user ,
both named in the configuration file
.Pq Sx FILES ,
which holds their tokens.
Without
.Ar user ,
the first user the file lists is the one notified.
.Pp
In the message,
.Ql %{HOST}
becomes the short host name,
.Ql %{HOSTNAME}
the full one, and any other
.Ql %{...}
is removed.
Backslashes and dollar signs arrive as typed.
.Pp
The tokens are handed to
.Xr curl 1
on its standard input, never on its command line, so they do not
appear in a process listing.
The message and the title are sent as form fields that curl never
reads as a file name: a message starting with
.Ql @
is sent as text.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "-t title"
.It Fl h
Print the usage and exit.
.It Fl t Ar title
The title of the notification.
.It Fl V
Print the version and exit.
.It Fl v
Once the notification is sent, report the request id Pushover gave
it, on stderr.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width PUSHOVER_CONFIG
.It Ev PUSHOVER_CONFIG
The configuration file, instead of
.Pa ~/.pushover .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.pushover
The tokens, in a YAML file of two levels: an
.Ql app\&:
section naming each application with its token, and a
.Ql user\&:
section naming each user with its key.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
app:
  myapp:  <application token>
user:
  me:     <user key>
.Ed
.Pp
A value may be quoted, with single or double quotes, and a
.Ql #
starts a comment.
A token must be letters and digits only; any other is refused.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
The notification was sent.
.It 1
It was not: the configuration file is missing, the user or the
application is not in it, a token is malformed, the message is empty,
curl failed, or the API refused it
.Po
with its error, or
.Dq message limit reached
for HTTP 429
.Pc .
.It 2
A usage error, an empty
.Ar user
or
.Ar app
in
.Ar user : Ns Ar app
among them.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Tell the default user that a backup is done, naming the host:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ pushover -t backup myapp 'done on %{HOST}'
.Ed
.Pp
Notify the user
.Ql me
from
.Ql myapp ,
and report the request id:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ pushover -v me:myapp 'disk almost full'
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr curl 1
.Pp
.Lk https://pushover.net/api
.Sh CAVEATS
Only the two-level layout shown in
.Sx FILES
is understood; the file is not read as YAML at large.
